  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Warming trend today through mid week. \n\n-  Thunderstorm chances expand northward Tuesday and Wednesday.\n   Gusty outflow winds and lightning as the main concerns. \n\n-  Cooler temperatures this weekend, shower/thunderstorm chances\n   continue. \n\n\nThrough Wednesday: High pressure will rebuild across the Northern\nRockies today, bringing stable conditions and light winds. \nTemperatures will trend warmer, peaking around 10 degrees above \nseasonal norms Tuesday and Wednesday. Air quality may degrade \nacross northwest Montana Tuesday and Wednesday as weak easterly \novernight flow transports smoke from the Camp Creek Fire into the \nregion.\n\nMonsoonal moisture will surge northward Tuesday, introducing \nshower and thunderstorm chances up to the I-90 corridor. Deeper \nmoisture will encompass most of the region Wednesday, expanding \nstorm coverage. A mix of wet and dry thunderstorms will heighten \nthe risk for lightning-initiated fire starts. Strong outflow winds\nwill accompany any activity, with an isolated storm or two \npotentially producing near-severe gusts (50-60 mph), primarily in \nsouthwest Montana on Wednesday.\n\nThursday through Weekend: Ensemble guidance maintains high \nconfidence (>90%) in a Pacific Northwest trough returning late \nthis week into the weekend. While exact timing and specific \nimpacts remain uncertain, expect moderating temperatures and an \nuptick in winds over several days, likely opening another window \nfor elevated fire weather. A minority but growing number of \nensemble solutions supports a closed-low track, which would yield \nmore widespread precipitation, a trend to monitor.",
